         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Nobel Prize winners for physics Robert W. Wilson, with beard, and Arno Penzias are shown on October 18, 1978 at Homedell Bell labs, New Jersey, U.S.A. in front of their microwave radio antenna. They won for studies in microwave radiation that tends to support "Big Bang" theory on creation of universe. (AP-PHOTO)</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
         <dc:title>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">ROBERT W. WILSON, ARNO PENZIAS</rdf:li>
