      </rdf:Description>
      <rdf:Description rdf:about=""
            xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">
         <dc:format>image/epsf</dc:format>
         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The three tenors from left: Jose Carreras, Luciano Pavarotti and  Placido Domingo pose for photographers during a press conference in Munich, Germany, Wednesday Oct. 11, 1995. The world's three top tenors announced Wednesday they will reunite for a five-date world tour beginning next summer.   The trio, who first teamed up for a charity concert in Rome in 1990, have outsold every other performer of classical music and have helped to popularize opera. Their second concert together was in Los Angeles last year to mark the World Cup soccer championship. (AP Photo/Uwe Lein)</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
         <dc:creator>
            <rdf:Seq>
               <rdf:li>UWE LEIN</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Seq>
         </dc:creator>
         <dc:title>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">GERMANY THREE TENORS PEOPLE</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:title>
         <dc:rights>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">AP1995</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:rights>
      </rdf:Description>
